delta-change "grammar-combinators"
message "install GrammarCombinators combinators precedence and associativity over ExpressionGrammar"
author "trellis-product"
doc "guide" """
  |# GrammarCombinators
  |
  |GrammarCombinators is the second grammar product successor after the frozen F0-F11 bootstrap constitution.
  |It is **not F12**.
  |
  |Derivation:
  |
  |```text
  |F11
  |  + LanguageBootstrap.delta = LanguageBootstrap
  |  + ExpressionGrammar.delta  = ExpressionGrammar
  |  + GrammarCombinators.delta  = GrammarCombinators
  |```
  |
  |## Purpose
  |
  |ExpressionGrammar removed the embedded `lit:...;ref:...` production mini-language. GrammarCombinators makes the expression graph itself more useful by adding:
  |
  |- `grammar.choice`
  |- `grammar.optional`
  |- `grammar.repeat`
  |- `grammar.precedence`
  |- `grammar.associativity`
  |
  |Choice alternatives, optional/repeat bodies, precedence, and associativity are all connected through typed Trellis edges. The Scala host contains a generic interpreter for those graph concepts rather than Bool0-specific parser branches.
  |
  |## Bool0 surface used for acceptance
  |
  |GrammarCombinators evolves the Bool0 surface to accept aliases and infix operators:
  |
  |```text
  |true | yes
  |false | no
  |! Expr | not Expr
  |Expr && Expr | Expr and Expr
  |Expr || Expr | Expr or Expr
  |( Expr )
  |```
  |
  |The graph defines binding strengths:
  |
  |```text
  |atom/group  100
  |prefix       80
  |&& / and     60   left associative
  ||| / or      40   left associative
  |```
  |
  |Thus:
  |
  |```text
  |! true && false || true
  |```
  |
  |parses as:
  |
  |```text
  |Or(And(Not(True), False), True)
  |```
  |
  |Parentheses are represented by an explicit `Group` constructor in this slice so round-trip printing never needs hidden host-side parenthesization rules.
  |
  |## Normalization policy
  |
  |Combinators also carry canonical printing policy as graph data.
  |
  |- a `choice` selects one canonical print alternative;
  |- an `optional` says whether its body prints canonically;
  |- a `repeat` gives a canonical print count.
  |
  |For example, GrammarCombinators deliberately accepts:
  |
  |```text
  |yes ; ; && no ?
  |```
  |
  |and normalizes it to:
  |
  |```text
  |true && false
  |```
  |
  |The punctuation is only an acceptance fixture showing that optional/repeat syntax can be interpreted without becoming AST structure.
  |
  |## Current deliberate restriction
  |
  |GrammarCombinators optional and repeat expressions must be capture-free. This keeps the existing `Tree` representation unchanged while establishing the graph semantics for the combinators. A later grammar product can introduce cardinality-aware AST fields rather than smuggling list/option semantics into the host.
  |
  |## Compatibility
  |
  |LanguageBootstrap and ExpressionGrammar remain separately materializable with their frozen roots. Their tests are pinned to `Language.language-bootstrap` and `Language.expression-grammar`; `Language.graph` now names the GrammarCombinators product successor.
  |
  |The independent Rust bootstrap verifier still stops at frozen F11. Product-language evolution must not alter bootstrap parity.
  |
  """
test "canonical delta contract"
  assert "canonical"
  assert "valid"
  assert "source-roundtrip"
  assert "dependency" "grammar-expression-graph"
  assert "introduces" "grammar.component.choice" "grammar.component"
depends "grammar-expression-graph"
  replace "grammar.component.choice" "grammar.component"
    port "self" "out" "3:cap4:meta12:unrestricted14:4:atom6:Schema6:4:none"
